|term[intermediate-location]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A step along a path that is itself a location, owning the routing of its next hop.
  |designation intermediate-location
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-locations-and-paths
    :anchor path
    :projection paraphrase
    Intermediate steps of a path may themselves be intermediate locations; each is in charge of routing from there — only that item is expected to know how to route to the next.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:il(l, p) := l \in steps(p) \land l \ne dst(p)>
    :reading Constitutive: an intermediate location is a non-terminal step of a path that is itself a location.
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @location
  ; Constitutive, not incidental: to BE an intermediate location is to be a
  ; non-terminal step of a path that is itself a location.
  |rel :kind step-of :to @path :card +
  |rel :kind performs :to @progressive-routing
